      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T04:55:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we just use a different enum mpu_region in mpu.h, instead of trying to look for an available region at runtime?",
      "revId": "21cdc2db621214beffd8ad780f2d08e656518e12",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79ee2d7b_cb7673ea",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T20:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could have a #define for the number of MPU regions and use that to choose either the single region or two regions, but this code is more generic and doesn\u0027t require (yet another) config option that someone might forget to enable (or set incorrectly).\n\nCombined with the rollback test that runs on device, it\u0027s easy to confirm that the right code is running here: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/test/rollback.c\n\n(I have a separate upcoming commit that flashes and runs all the unit tests to make sure they pass as described in: http://go/cros-fingerprint-automated-testing).\n\nI know there\u0027s always the size concern, but I\u0027d prefer to default to generic, maintainable, easy-to-read code first before trying to cut out every last byte before we\u0027ve hit a memory wall.",
      "parentUuid": "03850953_8526c1e6",
      "revId": "21cdc2db621214beffd8ad780f2d08e656518e12",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7da36aa_d65c1cca",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T23:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e this code is more generic and doesn\u0027t require (yet another) config option that someone might forget to enable (or set incorrectly).\n\nThis can be alleviated with BUILD_ASSERT. And you have tests too now.\n\nGenerally the EC philosophy is to do things at compile time.",
      "parentUuid": "79ee2d7b_cb7673ea",
      "revId": "21cdc2db621214beffd8ad780f2d08e656518e12",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cdea6851_dd8bde0b",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-21T00:32:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the \"always have everything at compile time\" ends up making the code incredibly hard to read as it scales  across different chips (tons of nested ifdefs and huge config files that are mostly copy/pasted).\n\nI\u0027m not sure I see the downside of doing something at runtime if it can be done correctly and generically (like this case).\n\nI\u0027ll defer to Jett since we don\u0027t seem to agree.",
      "parentUuid": "d7da36aa_d65c1cca",
      "revId": "21cdc2db621214beffd8ad780f2d08e656518e12",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5ea0c6d_2f4a7468",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/mpu.c",
